{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ADnSjKKujTzVCiCRc9TaKt","type":"tool_result","content":"29:        batch_ntt_small::ensure_device_ntt_twiddles_initialized,\n470:    /// SP_DEG=1 round 0: computes G0, G1, G2 on identity coset, then reconstructs s_0 on CPU.\n472:    /// Key insight: Instead of computing s₀(Z) directly on 2 cosets with in-kernel NTT,\n474:    /// reconstruct s₀ via CPU-side NTT-based polynomial multiplication.\n551:        // CPU reconstruction: s₀(Z) = E0(Z)*G0(Z) + E1(Z)*G1(Z) + E2(Z)*G2(Z)\n552:        let s_0 = self.reconstruct_s0_from_g(d_g_pos, d_g_neg, s_0_deg)?;\n558:    /// Reconstructs s_0 from G0, G1, G2 using NTT-based polynomial multiplication.\n566:    fn reconstruct_s0_from_g(\n588:            // NTT-based multiplication: s_0 += E0*G0 + E1*G1 + E2*G2\n643:    /// NTT-based polynomial multiplication following logup pattern.\n645:    fn ntt_multiply_and_add(\n1038:/// NTT-based polynomial multiplication\n1039:fn poly_multiply_ntt(dft: &Radix2BowersSerial, a: &[EF], b: &[EF], min_size: usize) -> Vec<EF> {"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_018EVqQzC5ECdWLpTMGrW7wm","session_id":"f4b22a1a-5187-493b-801a-a22317879818","uuid":"55289780-7db8-45be-ba2e-92a7ecd0981d","timestamp":"2026-04-15T03:42:44.572Z"}
