{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XYzWkW1irabD6AmvQGdqs9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-15-0800-arena-merkle-tree-digest-layers\n2\t\n3\tReplace the per-layer `DeviceBuffer` allocations in Merkle tree construction with a single arena allocation, reducing ~19 CUDA memory pool operations to 1 per tree. At APC 300, 12 Merkle trees are built per proof (2 trace commits + 10 WHIR rounds), creating ~228 separate digest buffer allocations. The first segment pays heavy allocation costs (seg 0 stacked_commit is 163ms vs seg 1's 87ms despite similar GPU kernel work), and every tree pays per-layer pool lookup overhead. A single arena allocation per tree eliminates this churn and is expected to reduce STARK excl trace by 30-60ms.\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Gyq7DFJwFwKQtVPkm2Sa3z","session_id":"f4b22a1a-5187-493b-801a-a22317879818","uuid":"875f0d81-235b-442c-9a52-481764957da1","timestamp":"2026-04-15T03:56:06.918Z"}
