{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GN9XCuGCzYxTS9KAibRWPy","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Plan: Bulk-Allocate MLE Fold Output Buffers\n2\t\n3\t## Goal\n4\t\n5\tEliminate ~37,000 per-round `cudaMallocAsync`/`cudaFreeAsync` calls in MLE sumcheck fold rounds by replacing per-matrix individual allocations with a single bulk allocation per fold group per round. This targets the main-thread allocation overhead visible in nsight (47K mallocs for 38ms + 49K frees for 21ms = 59ms total), which is the primary cause of MLE Rounds reverse-scaling at APC 300 (173ms vs 114ms at APC 0 despite 2x less total work).\n6\t\n7\t**Expected saving**: 40–55ms at APC 300 (MLE Rounds 173ms → ~118–133ms).\n8\t\n9\t**Scope**: Only the MLE fold loop (`fold_mle_evals`, rounds 1..n_max). The one-time `fold_ple_evals` (round 0, ~2500 allocs, ~2ms overhead) is NOT changed — it continues to use `DeviceMatrix<EF>` and is handled by a transitional type in the first MLE fold round.\n10\t\n11\t## Current Code Path\n12\t\n13\t### MLE round loop (`mod.rs:631–648`)\n14\t\n15\tEach round calls:\n16\t1. `sumcheck_polys_batch_eval(round, r[round-1])` — evaluates sumcheck polynomials for all traces\n17\t2. `compute_batch_s_poly(...)` — CPU batching\n18\t3. `fold_mle_evals(round, r_round)` — halves all trace matrix heights via GPU kernel\n19\t\n20\t### `fold_mle_evals` (`mod.rs:2000–2091`)\n21\t\n22\tThe inner `batch_fold` closure (line 2002–2048):\n23\t1. **Counts foldable matrices**: `partition_point(|mat| mat.height() > 1)` → `num_matrices`\n24\t2. **Allocates per-matrix output buffers** (line 2014):\n25\t   ```rust\n26\t   let output_mat = DeviceMatrix::<EF>::with_capacity(output_height, width);\n27\t   ```\n28\t   At APC 300: ~1246 matrices for mat_evals + ~623 for sels = **~1869 individual allocations per round**.\n29\t3. **Collects pointer arrays**, uploads 4 small H2D buffers (input_ptrs, output_ptrs, heights, widths)\n30\t4. **Single `batch_fold_mle` kernel launch** — one kernel folds all matrices"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Gyq7DFJwFwKQtVPkm2Sa3z","session_id":"f4b22a1a-5187-493b-801a-a22317879818","uuid":"42ce63dc-973f-4fee-801f-924e03352715","timestamp":"2026-04-15T03:57:08.507Z"}
