{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017HgSVAHdWoAmaojwyX5ZDY","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Plan: Drain GPU Pipeline Before STARK Timing Span\n2\t\n3\t## Goal\n4\t\n5\tEliminate GPU pipeline stall from async trace generation that inflates the `stark_prove_excluding_trace` timing metric. Per-segment analysis shows ~130ms stall in segment 0 and ~59ms stall in segment 1 at APC 300, totaling ~189ms — 15% of the measured 1301ms STARK excl trace. At APC 0, the stall is much smaller (~50-100ms across 5 segments) because trace gen launches fewer/simpler async GPU kernels (no `apc_apply_bus_kernel`). The fix disproportionately helps APC 300, improving the APC 0 / APC 300 scaling ratio toward the >2x target.\n6\t\n7\tEvidence for the pipeline stall:\n8\t- APC 300 seg0: `trace_gen_time_ms` = 755ms (CPU-side async kernel launches), `main_trace_commit_time_ms` = 164ms, but actual `stacked_commit` work is ~35ms (measured in debug run).\n9\t- The `apc_apply_bus_kernel` alone has 609ms total GPU time (583 instances) — this trace gen GPU work runs concurrently with CPU-side trace gen but extends past it, causing the stall.\n10\t- The stall also causes GPU resource contention: trace gen kernels competing with STARK kernels for SM time on the first STARK GPU operations.\n11\t\n12\t## Current Code Path\n13\t\n14\tThe `Coordinator::prove` function at `crates/stark-backend/src/prover/mod.rs:104-198` has an `#[instrument(name = \"stark_prove_excluding_trace\")]` attribute that starts the timing span at function entry. Inside the `stacked_commit` call chain, stream-ordered GPU operations (memsets, kernel launches) are enqueued after any pending trace gen kernels on the same per-thread CUDA stream (`cudaStreamPerThread`). The CPU-side synchronization that actually blocks occurs at `MerkleTreeGpu::root()` → `to_host()` (at `crates/cuda-backend/src/merkle_tree.rs:163`), which performs `cudaEventSynchronize` — this is where the CPU waits for ALL prior stream work to complete, including pending trace gen kernels.\n15\t\n16\t**Single-stream assumption**: This plan depends on trace gen kernels being launched on the same `cudaStreamPerThread` stream as the STARK prover (i.e., on the same OS thread). The measured stall inside `stacked_commit` (164ms span time vs ~35ms actual work in isolated runs) is empirical evidence that this is the case — if trace gen used different streams, `to_host()` would not block on them.\n17\t\n18\tThe `ProverDevice` trait is at `crates/stark-backend/src/prover/hal.rs:53-63`. It currently has no method for GPU synchronization.\n19\t\n20\tThe GPU backend implements `ProverDevice` at `crates/cuda-backend/src/gpu_backend.rs:76-83`. The `GpuDevice` struct has access to `current_stream_sync()` from `openvm_cuda_common::stream`.\n21\t\n22\tThe CPU backend implements `ProverDevice` at `crates/stark-backend/src/prover/cpu_backend.rs`. It needs no GPU synchronization.\n23\t\n24\t## Changes\n25\t\n26\t### 1. Add `drain_pending_device_ops` to `ProverDevice` trait\n27\t\n28\t**File**: `crates/stark-backend/src/prover/hal.rs`\n29\t\n30\tAdd a method to the `ProverDevice` trait with a default no-op implementation:\n31\t\n32\t```rust\n33\tpub trait ProverDevice<PB: ProverBackend, TS>:\n34\t    TraceCommitter<PB> + MultiRapProver<PB, TS> + OpeningProver<PB, TS>\n35\t{\n36\t    type Error: ...;\n37\t\n38\t    /// Drain any pending device operations from prior phases.\n39\t    /// Called before the STARK timing span to ensure accurate measurement.\n40\t    /// Default implementation is a no-op (for CPU backends).\n41\t    fn drain_pending_device_ops(&self) -> Result<(), Self::Error> { Ok(()) }\n42\t}\n43\t```\n44\t\n45\tThis is a backward-compatible change: all existing implementors get the no-op default. The `Result` return type matches the error-handling pattern used throughout the GPU backend (e.g., `ProverError::CurrentStreamSync` variant already exists).\n46\t\n47\t### 2. Implement `drain_pending_device_ops` for `GpuDevice`\n48\t\n49\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/gpu_backend.rs`\n50\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Gyq7DFJwFwKQtVPkm2Sa3z","session_id":"f4b22a1a-5187-493b-801a-a22317879818","uuid":"fd19d4b8-cf82-4f2a-9ac6-cf019dc2fc51","timestamp":"2026-04-15T03:57:50.469Z"}
