sured time is 83-100ms though, which is way higher than the 10-15ms I'd expect. I'm wondering if the metrics are capturing time from outside the `stack_traces` function itself—maybe there's other code in `stacked_commit` that I'm not accounting for. Let me look at the actual `stacked_commit` implementation to see what else is happening there.\n\nLooking at the function, I see it's doing the stacked matrix layout, then conditionally calling `stack_traces`, followed by `rs_code_matrix` and building a Merkle tree with GPU operations. The `MemTracker` is wrapping the whole thing, so the metrics should be capturing all of this work together.\n\nNow I'm wondering if the `MemTracker` operations themselves might be causing GPU synchronization — specifically, if `mem.tracing_info()` or `mem.emit_metrics()` are calling something like `cudaMemGetInfo` under the hood, that would force the GPU to wait for all pending work to finish, which could be expensive.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9225,"cache_read_input_tokens":208862,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9225},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f4b22a1a-5187-493b-801a-a22317879818","uuid":"39e85010-b909-4546-b8ad-76397da6bffa"}
