07:** **Round 0 BEGINS HERE**\n   - **Line 507:** First new transcript sample: `lambda = transcript.sample_ext()`\n   - This is the **first** randomness sampled in the Round 0 span\n   - All previous `xi` values are already fixed\n\n---\n\n### 3. **Exact Transcript Flow Between GKR and Round 0**\n\n**Between GKR input evals and Round 0, the transcript receives:**\n\n**File: `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/fractional.rs` (lines 491-501)**\n- `fractional_sumcheck_gpu()` observes intermediate sumcheck proofs and samples GKR `xi` values\n- **These are completely independent of Round 0 constraints**\n\n**File: `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs` (lines 490-507)**\n```rust\nlet (frac_sum_proof, mut xi) =\n    fractional_sumcheck_gpu(transcript, inputs, alpha, true, &mut prover.mem)?;  // LINE 490-491\nwhile xi.len() != l_skip + n_global {\n    xi.push(transcript.sample_ext());  // LINE 493\n}\ndebug!(?xi);\nprover.xi = xi;  // LINE 496 - xi is FIXED here\n\nlogup_gkr_span.exit();  // LINE 498 - GKR phase ends\n\nlet round0_span = info_span!(\"prover.rap_constraints.round0\", phase = \"prover\").entered();\nlet mut sumcheck_round_polys = Vec::with_capacity(n_max);\nlet mut r = Vec::with_capacity(n_max + 1);\nlet lambda = transcript.sample_ext();  // LINE 507 - FIRST Round 0 sample\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. **Could GKR Input Evaluation Run Concurrently with Round 0?**\n\n**NO - there is a logical, but NOT data, dependency:**\n\nThe code structure prevents concurrent execution because:\n\n1. **Lines 462-474:** `log_gkr_input_evals()` completes and returns\n2. **Lines 490-496:** `fractional_sumcheck_gpu()` must complete before Round 0 (they use sequential transcript samples)\n3. **Line 496:** `prover.xi` is set from GKR output\n4. **Line 518:** Round 0 immediately uses `prover.xi[..l_skip]` in `eq_sharp_uni_poly(&prover.xi[..l_skip])`\n5. **Line 573:** Round 0 uses `prover.xi[0]` in `eq_uni_poly::<F, _>(l_s